// `std.quantum`: the home of the qubit type. `Qubit` is one quantum bit, and it
// carries no comonoid: no binder copies or discards a qubit. Only a linear
// function's parameter holds one, so a gate is a linear function from `Qubit`
// to `Qubit`.
//
// A source names the type in its import list, `import std.quantum (Qubit);`.
// The atom is native, so no declaration here states it. The lowering answers
// it only in a source that imports it from this module.
//
// - see: #5739
